meta {
  name: Update Series
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/time-block-series/:seriesId
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  seriesId: PASTE_SERIES_ID_HERE
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "effectiveFrom": "2026-11-01",
    "pattern": {
      "type": "DAILY",
      "time": "10:00",
      "durationMinutes": 30
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Series (split forward)

  Split-forward edit: closes the current series the day before `effectiveFrom`
  and creates a new series starting at `effectiveFrom` with the new rule.
  History (occurrences before `effectiveFrom`) is never rewritten. Returns 200
  with the NEW series.

  Requires ACCESS_TOKEN cookie + X-CSRF-Token header
  (the `csrfToken` env var is auto-filled by the login/register/refresh
  post-response script — never paste it manually).

  Body: `effectiveFrom` (required, must be after the series startDate),
  plus any of `title`, `projectId`, `endDate`, `pattern` (same shape as
  create; omitted fields keep the old rule).

  Returns 400 INVALID_SERIES_RANGE when `effectiveFrom` is not after the
  series start, 400 INVALID_SERIES_PATTERN on bad pattern, 404 when the
  series (or projectId) does not belong to the user.

  NOTE: the backend log line "Request without Origin and Referer headers"
  is a harmless WARN (fail-open for non-browser clients like Bruno) — it does
  NOT block the request.
}
